From 1ab0737e9ffbce41f78971a0b0fd0f9f8b57e9fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 40/70] fix(dispatch): block re-dispatch and false-close of
 MQ-submitted beads (gfork-649)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of the an-abn false-close (2026-07-11): under merge_strategy=pr
the source bead stays open until its PR merges (hq-6wd2) and the polecat
session stops after gt done — so the convoy stranded scan (isReadyIssue)
saw every completed-but-unmerged bead as abandoned (open bead, dead
session) and re-fed it. The duplicate polecat then hit gt done's no-MR
path where the verified_push gate passes vacuously (zero commits, HEAD on
the master base) and force-closed the bead while the prior attempt's PR
was still open.

Three guards, all keyed on open merge-request beads (FindOpenMRsForIssue):

1. gt sling refuses beads with a clean open MR (no conflict/retry/close
   evidence) unless --force — the chokepoint for every dispatcher.
   Distressed-MR takeover (GH#gt-zqvj prior-attempt flow) still passes.
2. convoy stranded ready-list skips such issues so the daemon stops
   nominating them every scan.
3. gt done's no-MR close path skips close when ANY open MR references the
   issue — the refinery owns completion (false-close backstop).

Dispatch guards fail open on lookup errors (degrade to current behavior
when Dolt is down); the close guard is the safety net behind them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
